  "ingredients": [
    "0.5 cup mayonnaise",
    "2.5 teaspoons Cajun seasoning",
    "1 cup gluten-free panko bread crumbs",
    "1 (1 pound) fillet cod, cut into 4 pieces",
    "cooking spray"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Combine mayonnaise and Cajun seasoning in a small bowl. Place bread crumbs on a plate.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Spread Cajun mayonnaise on both sides of fish fillets with a small spatula or butter knife. Coat each fillet, one at a time, with bread crumbs. Lightly spray both sides of breaded fillets with cooking spray and transfer 2 fillets to each air fryer tray; do not overcrowd.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn an air fryer to the Roast setting (375 degrees F (190 degrees C) according to manufacturer's instructions and set timer to 14 minutes. Rotate trays at 7 minutes. Fish should flake easily with a fork.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Carefully remove fillets from the trays and serve.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    }
  ],
